  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You love array, don't you?\n\nYou are given two integer NNN and MMM, along with an array BBB of length NNN containing **pairwise distinct** integers. You have to find the number of array AAA of length NNN satisfying the follow conditions:\n\n\n1≤Ai≤M1 \\leq A_i \\leq M1≤Ai​≤M.\nAi≠AjA_i \\neq A_jAi​=Aj​ for all 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N.\nAi≠BiA_i \\neq B_iAi​=Bi​ for all 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N.\nSince the answer can be very large, output it under modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM.\nThe second line of the input contains NNN separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\dots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​ - the array BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput on a single line the number of satisfactory array modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤M≤3⋅1051 \\leq M \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤M≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Bi≤1091 \\leq B_i \\leq 10^91≤Bi​≤109",
      "Bi≠BjB_i \\neq B_jBi​=Bj​ for all 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
